    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d307">

                <pb facs="0425" n="319" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg319"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary of State Bacon to Minister
                        Rockhill.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-07-13"><hi rendition="#italic">July 13,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Rockhill is informed that Consul-General Lay has wired that the viceroy paid
                    compensation for the losses at Lienchou, as claimed. The department assumes that
                    this settlement will not preclude claims <pb facs="0426" n="320" xml:id="pg320"
                    /> as stated in its telegram to Mr. Rockhill of June 8. These claims are about
                    to be presented, being now in a final form. Mr. Bacon requests an immediate
                    reply.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
